@startuml fulfillment-state
title Fulfillment — Canonical V1 Lifecycle
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> PLANNED
PLANNED --> ALLOCATED
ALLOCATED --> PICKING
PICKING --> PICKED
PICKED --> PACKED
PACKED --> STAGED
STAGED --> READY_FOR_DISPATCH
READY_FOR_DISPATCH --> HANDED_OVER
HANDED_OVER --> COMPLETED

ALLOCATED --> SHORTAGE : allocation shortage
PICKING --> SHORTAGE : pick discrepancy
PICKING --> HOLD : operational hold
STAGED --> HOLD : operational hold
PLANNED --> CANCELLED : cancel
HOLD --> CANCELLED : cancel

COMPLETED --> [*]
SHORTAGE --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]

note right of HOLD
HOLD and SHORTAGE require an explicit owning
workflow decision; this diagram does not invent
a universal recovery transition.
end note
@enduml
